Frontend feature-gate fix. Found during a consistency audit vs Docker/Ollama/Telegram: Docker and Ollama are always compiled in, but android is feature-gated (off by default) — yet the frontend is one build that always rendered the Android nav + connector tile. In a default build, adding an android connector hit create_connector's cfg-gated-out android arm and fell through to the WebhookConnector fallback (silent wrong-type). Fix consumes the feature_enabled flag (which we added in 09f4a03, NOT pre-existing — Docker's check_docker has no such field) from /api/setup/check-android-sdk: nav link in +layout.svelte and the add-tile in settings/connectors gated on it; full connectorTypes kept for icon lookups. Audit verdict: android otherwise faithfully mirrors Docker's check/start lifecycle (and neither auto-starts via reconciler — both user-triggered via frontend; my earlier note claiming Docker auto-starts was wrong). Minor unfixed: lifecycle is_running hardcodes emulator-5554 so a BYO device on another serial wont show as available in the start-gate; connector status still point-in-time. Frontend build verified.
